    "id": "train-1925",
    "question": "Tyson can swim at a speed of 3 miles per hour in a lake and 2.5 mph in an ocean. This season, half his races happened in lakes and half his races happened in the ocean. He had ten total races, each of which was 3 miles long. How much time did he spend in his races?",
    "gold": "11",
    "answer": "He did 5 races in the lake because 10 / 2 = <<10/2=5>>5\nHe did 5 races in the ocean because 10 / 2 = <<10/2=5>>5\nHe raced 15 miles in the lake because 5 x 3 = <<5*3=15>>15\nHis lake races took 6 hours because 15 / 2.5 = <<15/2.5=6>>6\nHe raced 15 miles in the ocean because 5 x 3 = <<5*3=15>>15\nHis ocean races took 5 hours because 15 / 3 = <<15/3=5>>5\nHe spent 11 hours racing because 5 + 6 = <<5+6=11>>11\n#### 11"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total time Tyson spent in his races, we need to break down the problem into smaller steps.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of races in each environment:**\n   Since half of his races happened in lakes and half in the ocean, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of races in lakes} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of races in the ocean} = \\frac{10}{2} = 5\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the time spent in each type of race:**\n   - **Time spent in lakes:**\n     Tyson swims in lakes at a speed of 3 miles per hour. Each race is 3 miles long. The time spent in each lake race is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Time per lake race} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{3 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 1 \\text{ hour}\n     \\]\n     Since he had 5 lake races, the total time spent in lake races is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total time in lake races} = 5 \\times 1 \\text{ hour} = 5 \\text{ hours}\n     \\]\n   - **Time spent in the ocean:**\n     Tyson swims in the ocean at a speed of 2.5 miles per hour. Each race is 3 miles long. The time spent in each ocean race is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Time per ocean race} = \\frac{3 \\text{ miles}}{2.5 \\text{ miles per hour}} = 1.2 \\text{ hours}\n     \\]\n     Since he had 5 ocean races, the total time spent in ocean races is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total time in ocean races} = 5 \\times 1.2 \\text{ hours} = 6 \\text{ hours}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total time spent in all races:**\n   The total time spent in all races is the sum of the time spent in lake races and the time spent in ocean races:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total time} = 5 \\text{ hours} + 6 \\text{ hours} = 11 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total time Tyson spent in his races is \\(\\boxed{11}\\) hours.",
